    "result_text": "The build is green. The test suite passes (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, `BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `telephoneDisplay` \u2014 the stored E.164 telephone formatted for humans \u2014 while keeping `telephone` as raw E.164.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `telephoneDisplay` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema (the `OwnerDto` is generated from this spec at build time).\n\n2. **`TelephoneNormalizer.java`** \u2014 Added a `toDisplayForm(String e164Telephone)` method that splits the number into its country code (`+61`) and national digits, then groups the national digits in threes from the left, joined by a space: `+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`. It reuses the existing private `countryCodeOf`/`nationalNumberOf` helpers, returns `null` for null/non-`+` input, and returns the number unchanged if its country code isn't one it recognizes.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Injected the `TelephoneNormalizer` and added a `@Mapping` for `telephoneDisplay` that calls `telephoneNormalizer.toDisplayForm(owner.getTelephone())`, consistent with the other derived-field mappings.\n\nThe acceptance test confirms `$.telephone` stays `+61412345678` while `$.telephoneDisplay` is `+61 412 345 678`.",
